# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bulk regenerable data — deliberately NOT committed (~2.9 GB).
#
# interp.csv are the 100x-finer continuous-time trajectory dumps (59,900 rows
# per run, ~14 MB each, 120+ runs). They are the raw input to the qualitative
# 3D panels (Figs 1, 7, 15-18) and are fully regenerated by:
#     reproduction/scripts/run_sweeps.sh
#     reproduction/scripts/run_figure_01_10_torus_substitute.sh
# Everything needed to READ the results without rerunning is committed:
# the rendered figures, all summary.csv, the digitised paper data, and the
# 790-row master table reproduction_summary.csv.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/**/interp.csv
results/**/nees_per_pose.csv
results/**/iteration_times.csv
results/**/*.log
